zotero-bridge-setup-welcome-title = Welcome to ZotMax
zotero-bridge-setup-welcome-lead = ZotMax is a plugin for Zotero: it brings the papers you collect, your PDF highlights, notes and appraisals into your own Obsidian or Notion.
zotero-bridge-setup-welcome-find = Finding literature and writing stay with you; it only helps with the chores: organising, tracking and appraising.
zotero-bridge-setup-welcome-ai = AI only appears after you turn it on yourself and add an API key.
zotero-bridge-setup-welcome-switch = Every feature can be turned off, any time, in Settings → ZotMax.
zotero-bridge-setup-welcome-time = About 3 minutes: pick a mode, connect your notes, AI (optional), then sync one paper to see it work. Every step can be skipped.
zotero-bridge-setup-mode-title = Pick a starting point
zotero-bridge-setup-mode-lead = The two modes differ in which features start on. You can change this in Settings → Features, or switch features one by one.
zotero-bridge-setup-mode-recommended = Recommended for new users
zotero-bridge-setup-mode-custom = Your switches are “Custom” now; leave both unselected to keep them as they are.
zotero-bridge-setup-mode-saved = Switched to “{ $name }”.
zotero-bridge-setup-notes-title = Where should your notes go?
zotero-bridge-setup-notes-lead = When you sync, every paper becomes one note, in the place you choose.
zotero-bridge-setup-notes-obsidian = Obsidian
zotero-bridge-setup-notes-obsidian-desc = Notes are Markdown files on your computer, in your vault folder.
zotero-bridge-setup-notes-notion = Notion
zotero-bridge-setup-notes-notion-desc = Every paper is a page in a Notion database; syncing goes online.
zotero-bridge-setup-notes-both = Both
zotero-bridge-setup-notes-both-desc = Obsidian and Notion are updated together.
zotero-bridge-setup-notes-none = Not now
