zotero-bridge-setup-notion-lead = Notion needs three things: an integration token, a database, and the integration connected to that database.
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-step1 = At notion.so/profile/integrations, create an Internal integration and copy its token (starts with ntn_).
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-step2 = Create a database in Notion (an empty Table is fine), then ••• at the top right → Connections → add the integration.
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-step3 = Copy the database link and paste it below.
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-howto = See the illustrated steps on the website
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-token = Integration token
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-token-saved = A token is already stored; leave this empty to keep it.
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-database = Database link
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-test = Test Connection
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-testing = Testing…
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-test-hint = Testing saves the token and the link first, and adds the columns ZotMax needs to the database.
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-need-token = Please paste the Notion integration token.
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-bad-database = This doesn’t look like a Notion database link: it needs a 32-character ID. Open the database in Notion and copy its address.
zotero-bridge-setup-notion-failed = Connection failed: { $error }
zotero-bridge-setup-ai-title = AI literature notes (optional)
zotero-bridge-setup-ai-lead = When you sync, an AI can draft a reading note for each paper first: study design, sample, PICO, a first appraisal, for you to check.
zotero-bridge-setup-ai-cost = It uses your own API key and is billed by usage, paid directly to Anthropic or OpenAI; ChatGPT or Claude subscriptions don’t work here.
zotero-bridge-setup-ai-optional = You can do without AI entirely: syncing, highlights and appraisal forms all work. If you’re not sure, skip this.
